WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.071 --> 00:00:13.565
"Rise and shine!" the computer announced. "It's time to get up!"

2
00:00:13.566 --> 00:00:17.015
Ally yawned.

3
00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:20.595
"And you know what that means," the computer continued.

4
00:00:20.596 --> 00:00:27.846
"I sure do, Alpha," Ally said as the computer's lights started blinking and dance music blared from speakers.

5
00:00:27.847 --> 00:00:30.364
"Dance party!" the computer said.

6
00:00:30.365 --> 00:00:34.942
Ally leaped out of bed and danced around the pod.

7
00:00:34.943 --> 00:00:38.563
"Do the Kleptorian twist," the computer called out.

8
00:00:38.564 --> 00:00:41.798
Ally did a twisty dance move.

9
00:00:41.799 --> 00:00:45.216
"Now the Jardonian tango."

10
00:00:45.217 --> 00:00:51.683
Ally laughed as she changed up her moves. "I love starting the day this way!"

11
00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:58.642
"Evidence indicates that dancing is excellent for waking up the Astralian brain and body," the computer said.

12
00:00:58.643 --> 00:01:05.456
Ally danced over to a storage hatch and removed a small box. She placed it on the table.

13
00:01:05.457 --> 00:01:12.069
"You can turn off the music now," she said. "I'm wide awake and ready to count my money." The

14
00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:15.464
computer fell silent as Ally pulled money out of the box. Using

15
00:01:15.465 --> 00:01:22.721
her superior mathematic abilities, she flipped through the bills and added them up in just a few seconds. "Eight

16
00:01:22.722 --> 00:01:25.635
hundred and thirty-five," she said. "This

17
00:01:25.636 --> 00:01:30.202
is more than enough to buy the parts and fuel we need to get back home. I

18
00:01:30.203 --> 00:01:35.287
never thought I'd say this, Alpha, but I can't wait to see my parents. Can

19
00:01:35.288 --> 00:01:38.329
you tell me exactly what I need to buy?" The

20
00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:44.895
computer's lights flashed. "Printing out a list of parts and the exact weight of the fuel cells." Ally

21
00:01:44.896 --> 00:01:50.992
grabbed the printout. "Great! Now I need to find the time to go buy everything. Ever

22
00:01:50.993 --> 00:01:59.652
since the diner reopened, I haven't had any time off." ***

23
00:01:59.653 --> 00:02:06.202
When Ally got to the diner, Randy, a new assistant cook, was grilling in the kitchen while Mateo ate breakfast at the counter.

24
00:02:06.203 --> 00:02:09.737
His face was buried in his phone.

25
00:02:09.738 --> 00:02:13.153
"Texting with Bethany again?" Ally teased.

26
00:02:13.154 --> 00:02:22.857
Mateo blushed. "We're making plans to go to the sci-fi convention on Friday. You're coming with us, right?"

27
00:02:22.858 --> 00:02:28.202
"Do you always ask others to join your dates?" Ally asked.

28
00:02:28.203 --> 00:02:31.935
"No . . ." Mateo gave her a funny look.

29
00:02:31.936 --> 00:02:35.475
"It's kind of a group thing—Kate is coming.

30
00:02:35.476 --> 00:02:43.130
And the convention is really fun. It's got rides, an alien costume contest, and cool exhibits."

31
00:02:43.131 --> 00:02:47.262
"Um, I'll think about it," Ally said quickly.

32
00:02:47.263 --> 00:02:50.345
She couldn't tell Mateo, but she planned to be gone by Friday. She

33
00:02:50.346 --> 00:02:56.301
felt a sharp pang. "I'm really going to miss him," she thought. Ally

34
00:02:56.302 --> 00:02:59.720
was relieved when Ray called her into the office a second later. She

35
00:02:59.721 --> 00:03:05.742
didn't want Mateo to see her teary-eyed. "Good

36
00:03:05.743 --> 00:03:10.688
morning, Ray," Ally said. "Ready for another busy day?" "Yes,

37
00:03:10.689 --> 00:03:15.070
especially since I have Randy helping in the kitchen," Ray said. "Now

38
00:03:15.071 --> 00:03:17.537
we have to hire more waitstaff to help you. Can

39
00:03:17.538 --> 00:03:21.684
you help out with the interviews? You know the job better than anyone." "No

40
00:03:21.685 --> 00:03:26.307
problem," Ally said. She was secretly glad Ray had asked her. Now

41
00:03:26.308 --> 00:03:29.524
she could be sure that Ray had great help after she was gone. As

42
00:03:29.525 --> 00:03:34.969
Ally turned to leave the office, she noticed Ray staring at the photo on his desk again. "I

43
00:03:34.970 --> 00:03:37.857
don't want to read his mind," she thought. "It

44
00:03:37.858 --> 00:03:40.544
feels wrong for something so personal. But

45
00:03:40.545 --> 00:03:46.177
why does he always look so sad when he stares at that photo?" ***

46
00:03:46.178 --> 00:03:50.877
Ally interviewed job candidates all day long, although she kept thinking of it as inner

47
00:03:50.878 --> 00:03:55.906
-viewing. She read all the candidates' minds to see who had the nicest thoughts about the diner and working for

48
00:03:55.907 --> 00:04:02.522
Ray. "Ray needs people who will really care about the job," Ally

49
00:04:02.523 --> 00:04:05.192
thought. She was relieved when she interviewed a woman named

50
00:04:05.193 --> 00:04:08.265
Flo. Flo had lots of experience working in busy

51
00:04:08.266 --> 00:04:12.526
diners. "I just love serving good food to people!" she

52
00:04:12.527 --> 00:04:16.119
said. Flo also loved the new space theme at Ray's

53
00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:20.225
Diner. After Ally talked to Ray, he decided to hire Flo on the spot.

54
00:04:20.226 --> 00:04:26.616
Ally grinned. "If I train her today, I can take tomorrow morning off to go shopping," she thought.

55
00:04:26.617 --> 00:04:30.794
"This is working out great for everyone!"

56
00:04:30.795 --> 00:04:34.364
The last interview of the day was with a teenager named Barry.

57
00:04:34.365 --> 00:04:40.801
"I hope you'll hire me!" Barry said eagerly. "Ray's Diner is so unique and successful!"

58
00:04:40.802 --> 00:04:46.459
When Ally read his mind, she could see that Barry desperately wanted the job.

59
00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:51.285
"Wow," Ally thought, "getting this job means so much to him."

60
00:04:51.286 --> 00:04:58.502
Just then Ray came over. "I love your enthusiasm, Barry. You're hired!"

61
00:04:58.503 --> 00:05:03.253
Barry whooped and ran out of the diner.

62
00:05:03.254 --> 00:05:15.858
Ally and Ray looked at each other and laughed. "I guess that means he'll take the job!" Ally said.

